# ============================================================================
# SSVMAC / Maupo — publish contract
#
# The repo publishes THE WORK: code, mind (persona), face art, tests, CI.
# The repo never publishes THE LIFE: conversation logs, learned facts,
# energy state, snapshots — everything Maupo became while running stays
# local. A fresh clone must build and test cleanly; it must NOT contain
# anyone's conversations, ever.
# ============================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Maupo's private life — runtime state, never public
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# memory/: sessions/ (every conversation), soft/hard memory, vitality,
# health.log, and all hidden caches (.recall_cache.json, .semantic_index.json…)
memory/
# snapshots/: the 6-hour emergency snapshots of memory/ + mind/
snapshots/
# archived memory folders
memory_archive_*/
# compressor backups (soft_mem.md.bak)
*.bak
# any future runtime logs
*.log
# loader skips files starting with _ (working/reference art)
ui/face_assets/_*
# auto-generated every turn by the emotion engine (seeded on first run)
mind/emotional_matrix.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local secrets & environment — defensive, even though Maupo is keyless
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.local

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python tooling & caches
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.venv/
venv/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / agent / OS junk
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/
.freebuff/
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.tmp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Personal notes & talking points (not required to run Maupo)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
think_about_ssvmac.txt

